======

Kalsa Brain contains code derived from Jan (https://github.com/janhq/jan).

    package:  tauri-plugin-llamacpp v0.4.0
    manifest: authors = ["Jan <service@jan.ai>"]
              license = "MIT"

Jan's repository-level NOTICE says "Copyright 2025 Menlo Research". The plugin
directory ships no licence file of its own, so the MIT declaration in its
Cargo.toml is the one this attribution relies on.

Derived in `crates/kalsa-supervisor/src/child.rs`:

  * the Windows kill-on-close job object (`JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE`),
    from Jan's `src/engine/worker.rs`, module `reap`;
  * stdin as the shutdown signal (piped stdin, closed to ask the child to stop)
    and the working directory pinned to the binary's directory, from the same
    `spawn` function;
  * the SIGTERM-then-SIGKILL escalation shape, from Jan's `src/process.rs`.

Everything else in this repository was written here. No code was taken from
Jan's TypeScript packages (`core/`, `extensions/`), which are AGPL-3.0.

